 - [outer-loop] Wrote `results/operational_retro_2026_06_365.json` (schema `carnot.operational_retro.v64`). The authoritative timing source reports no experiment commits since activation of 2026.06.365, leaving `total_wall_time_minutes=0`, `experiments_completed=0`, `compute_bound_experiments_count=0`, `slowest_experiments=[]`, and `gpu_idle_on_compute_bound_tasks=null`. Both RTX 3090s idle is correct (0 compute-bound tasks) and is NOT flagged as a bottleneck. The milestone stalled at the .365 capstone aggregation gate (repeated pre-gate-block commits, no upstream experiment artifacts). Highest-leverage fix: a zero-artifact circuit-breaker plus capstone gate fall-through so a stalled milestone is surfaced early and still produces forward artifacts.
 - 2026-06-09: Archive .365 -> activate .366; GREEN-GATE: assert research-complete.yaml + ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml parse under yaml.safe_load, the ARC substrate unit tests are green, and the ARC agentic modules import (carnot.agentic.arc_agi3_world_model, arc_world_model_synth, arc_world_model_dsl), so .366 can EXECUTE the ARC accuracy + efficiency tasks. RECORD the .365 truth: exp3946 SOLVED r11l L1 (real-env-confirmed); exp3947/3948/3949/3950 never ran; exp3951 capstone blocked on op:exists. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: archived_v365_v366_active_first_solve_recorded_arc_substrate_green; results/experiment_3952_archive_v365_activate_v366.json
 - 2026-06-09: SECOND ARC-AGI-3 game solve: solve level-0 of the next-easiest NON-SPATIAL game (lp85-305b61c3 is known-tractable — EWM solves it 100%; su15-1944f8ab / sc25-635fd71a / tn36-ef4dde99 are candidates) via the perception -> induced-model -> goal-predicate loop that produced the r11l first solve. A SECOND solved game is the first evidence the method GENERALIZES beyond r11l (one solve could be game-specific luck; two is a method). Real-env-confirmed; pick the game empirically by L0 action budget + inducibility, do NOT hardcode the win from source. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: second_game_solve_lp85-305b61c3_levels1_solvedTrue; results/experiment_3954_second_game_solve.json
+- 2026-06-09: OWED from .365: induce a GOAL-PREDICATE from observed level-up transitions. The M2-v5 finding is that a trustworthy transition-model is necessary but NOT sufficient — you also need to RECOGNIZE the WIN state. Collect level-up transitions (via active/goal-directed play on the non-spatial games), characterize the grid-state property that holds at a win (e.g. all pieces on targets / a matched pattern), and emit a reusable goal_predicate(grid)->bool. Measure: on a held-out set, does the induced predicate correctly flag win-vs-non-win states (precision/recall)? Require >=2 level-up examples before committing a predicate (single-example goal mis-induction is the named M1/M2 risk). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: precision_0.40_recall_1.00; results/experiment_3956_goal_predicate_induction.json
